Description
{{more citations needed section|date=September 2023}}
Flowering dogwood is a small deciduous tree growing to {{convert|10|m|ft|abbr=on}} high, often wider than it is tall when mature, with a trunk diameter of up to {{convert|30|cm|ft|0|abbr=on}}. A 10-year-old tree will stand about {{convert|5|m|ft|0|abbr=on}} tall. The leaves are opposite, simple, ovate, {{convert|6|–|13|cm|abbr=on}} long and {{convert|4|–|6|cm|abbr=on}} broad, with an apparently entire margin (actually very finely toothed, under a lens); they turn a rich red-brown in fall.
